---
/* The third drawing: the evidence rule, which is the site's own mechanism.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Smaller than the other two because it illustrates one sentence — how a
   number gets onto a page here — and sits under "How to read this" as the
   picture of that section's paragraph. `corpus.json` is set in mono because
   it is a real file's name, which is machine truth in the ordinary way; the
   word "fails" is red because a failed build is a status, and status is the
   only job semantic colour has here. */
---

<figure class="fig-evidence">
  <div
    class="chain"
    role="img"
    aria-label="How a figure reaches a page: the run store is harvested, the harvest recomputes corpus.json, a page names a key from it, and a key the corpus does not have fails the build. The sentence never contains the value."
  >
    <span class="box" aria-hidden="true">run store</span>
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <span class="box" aria-hidden="true">harvest recomputes</span>
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <span class="box mono" aria-hidden="true">corpus.json</span>
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <span class="box" aria-hidden="true">a page names a key</span>
    <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <span class="box" aria-hidden="true">a missing key <span class="red">fails</span> the build</span>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    The sentence never contains the value, so the value cannot drift from the
    store it came out of.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-evidence {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .chain {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .box {
    border: var(--rule);
    background: var(--mantle);
    padding-block: var(--space-3xs);
    padding-inline: var(--space-2xs);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .mono {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--text-micro);
  }

  .red {
    color: var(--red);
  }

  .arrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--muted);
    max-inline-size: var(--measure);
  }
</style>
